  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1200 PM MDT Tue Oct 20 2026\n\nA large upper trough will continue spinning away off the coast of\nCalifornia. Meanwhile an upper high is to our southeast. This \nwill focus moisture and chances for storms over AZ and our western\nportions of the CWA Wednesday. A Marginal Risk is out tomorrow \nhighlighting the Continental Divide and west for strong storms \nthat could produce severe hail and severe wind gusts. The \naforementioned trough lifts out over the Lower CO Basin Thursday \nbut this will spell a very active couple days for the area with \npotential for flooding, and strong storms that could produce hail \nand severe wind gusts. Abnormally moist conditions on the way \nThursday where PWs will reach up to 1.1\" to 1.2\" which is record \nbreaking, or at least near record breaking, which will add to the \nflooding threat.\n\nBehind the main aforementioned trough, another low cuts off and \ngives us a little more energy for Saturdays storms. Continued rain\nand thunderstorm chances Saturday where severe thunderstorms are \npossible once again, as well as flooding. By the end of the \nweekend, this trough finally gets sucked into the main flow \nallowing some drier and clearing conditions from west to east. \nAnother strong cold front possible Monday into Tuesday with windy \nconditions.",
